{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Aaron returned, etc., and the plague was checked.</b> It returns to say <b>and the plague was checked</b> after it already said ״וַתֵּעָצַר הַמַּגֵּפָה״, to say that even after the cloud of incense had dissipated and Aaron returned to Moses, the plague remained checked — lest you say that it was checked only as long as the cloud of incense was rising, in the manner of what it says (Exodus 17:11): ״כַּאֲשֶׁר יָרִים מֹשֶׁה יָדוֹ״ etc." "<b>Further</b>, it may be explained according to the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory (Tanhuma, Korah 12), who said that the Destroyer did not accept [the authority] of Aaron, for Aaron said to it: ״I am the emissary of the Omnipresent,״ until he brought it to the entrance of the Tent of Meeting and it heard from the mouth of the Shekhinah. And this is what the verse says — <b>and the plague</b>, meaning: the angel of destruction is called ״plague,״ and it too agreed to be checked. And therefore it carefully says <b>and the plague was checked</b>, whereas above it said <b>וַתֵּעָצַר הַמַּגֵּפָה</b> — meaning, there was a restraint imposed upon it by Aaron, but it did not wish to be restrained; whereas afterward, the plague itself also agreed to be checked."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:10:43.737958522Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}